  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilient Agriculture: transforming the livelihoods of 32,800 poor women and men in Kitui</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to achieve improved livelihoods security for poor women, men and children from hazard-prone and/or marginalised rural communities in Kitui-Kenya.

An integrated approach will be used to increase the productivity and resilience of agricultural systems; consolidate engagement in markets and diversify income generation; as well as strengthening their adaptation to climate change, and increasing the ability of local small scale food producers to access services and influence development practices.</narrative>
  </description>
